# Planned ON a 5560U, on radiod's own core (CPU 8) at its production
# 3.2 GHz pin, with the production resctrl partition in force
# (/sys/fs/resctrl/radiod L3:0=3ff = 5.00 MiB).  FFTW picks algorithms by
# timing them, so a plan is only optimal on the machine it was measured
# on -- the 5560U's ten ways are 5 MiB where the 5825U's are 10 MiB, and
# that changes the answer.
#
# Measured worth, same silicon and isolation, 2026-10-02:
#   WB6CXC-7  this file (302 codelets, local)   fft 48.1%  (2 web clients)
#   AI6VN     5825U seed (206 codelets)         fft 59.0%  (0 web clients)
# ~11 points, and CXC carried the heavier client load.
#
# Converged: /var/lib/ka9q-radio/fft.log stays EMPTY across a full restart,
# so radiod asks for nothing this lacks -- including all 23 ka9q-web zoom
# levels (ka9q-web.c:716) and the demod channel-filter sizes.
# Harvested from WB6CXC-7 2026-10-02.
